WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:02.868
-Well, I guess
all's well that ends --

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.033
-It's them over there.
-[Bleep]

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.968
Okay, this piazza is famously
full of pigeons.

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.567
We run straight at them,
and when they take flight,

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.267
they'll hide us in a canopy
of wings and feathers.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:10.901
-Sounds good.
Let's go.

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:15.367
[ Crunching ]
-They're not flying.

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.400
-Why won't they fly?
-We're just crunching them.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.901
-I can hear their tiny,
brittle bones beneath my feet.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:22.100
-Oh, God.
I think I just curbed one.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.501
Are we going to hell for this?

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:25.434
-I have now killed
like 4,000 pigeons.

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.267
-I will never not feel them
under my feet.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:29.534
-And we're leaving a perfect
pigeon carcass path

00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:30.701
for the Caesars to follow.

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:33.367
-It's disgusting
and hurting our cause.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:34.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.300
-We're back with Andy Samberg.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.067
That was a clip from "Digman!"

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:40.367
This is very exciting.

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.100
I've watched the first
couple of episodes.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.067
You play an archeologist?
-I do.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.868
-Also known as an arky.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:47.067
That's what they call
each other in the show.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:48.567
-Yes. Ad nauseam.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:52.300
-And this is a --
kind of a Nick Cage voice.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.100
Is that a safe assumption?

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.267
-I would say it was birthed
from my Nick Cage impression.

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:58.734
-Yeah.
-Yeah, and then

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:01.934
now has become its own
entire world, which is fun.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:04.601
-It's really fun.
This show is full of jokes,

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:06.701
which I know is something
you take very seriously.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:09.367
-Thank you for saying that.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.100
-And a really fun cast.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.367
A lot of our friends are in it,

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:15.834
and that must be
just so much fun, as well.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.634
-It's a treat and a delight,

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:19.901
and I hope everyone on earth,

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.701
literally every person
on earth, watches it.

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.200
-Yeah.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.334
It's also --
It's on Comedy Central,

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:28.567
and it's really fun
because I feel like

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:31.033
at some point
the rules just changed

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:35.400
and it's so -- the language
is so delightfully filthy.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.033
-Yes.
Well, it's a lot like --

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:41.934
The rules have changed
in the world, you know.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.367
-Oh, wow,
This is so deep.

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:45.234
-[ Groans ]

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:47.434
Honestly, I put a lot of energy
in the first segment,

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:49.200
and I just ran out of gas.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:54.968
Full -- Just hit the wall.

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:58.167
Like, I don't know, man.
My kids woke up at like 4:00.

00:01:58.167 --> 00:01:59.734
-Your kids don't live
in New York.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:02.234
-No, no.
I slept alone last night.

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:04.467
[ Laughter ]
Whoo!

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:05.734
It was nice, too.
-Yeah, great.

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:08.968
-Yeah, I got
that good hotel blanket.

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:11.801
-You -- There was an article
about you in "The New Yorker."

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:13.567
And one of the exciting things
about "The New Yorker"

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:15.801
is they do a little bit of art,
a cartoon, if you will.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.400
-Yes, they do
the caricature of you,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.534
which going in I knew I was
gonna have feelings about.

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:22.534
But you're also just like --
But it's an honor

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:24.567
'cause it's "The New Yorker,"
so I did get mine.

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:27.434
-And how do you feel about it?
-I feel interesting.

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:31.434
-Okay. That's what
"The New Yorker" came up with.

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:33.234
Now, you saw this, though,
and you actually thought

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:35.767
there was somebody --
It made you think -- Not --

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:36.868
It didn't look like somebody.

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:38.400
-No, it immediately
made me think,

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.367
"This is a person Fred has,
like, a voice for."

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.901
Fred, have you seen it?
Do you see this guy?

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.934
-I see.
-Okay.

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:48.033
-[Dopey voice]
Uh, you guys open?

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:50.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.000
-That was the voice.
That was the voice.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:01.534
-"You guys open?"

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.434
-Yeah.
-One more, Fred. One more.

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:06.033
-It says you close at 5:00.

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.634
[ Normal voice ]
Because of the jaw.

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:08.767
There's, like, a --

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:11.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:14.167
-It's the jacket that really
makes it that guy.

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:16.868
-Yeah.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:19.467
Alright, buddy, well, what
a delight to have you here.

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:21.667
-Always a treat. Love you.
-Thank you so much.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.901
It's very nice to know that
if anything should happen to me,

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.767
God forbid, the show will be
in safe hands.

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:29.200
-Thank you so much.
Yes, I'll be ready and willing.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.100
Again, I got nothing left.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.400
I'm truly gonna walk offstage
and pass out on the floor.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.834
-Andy Samberg, everybody.

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:39.234
"Digman!" is so funny.

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:41.434
It airs Wednesday nights
at 10:30

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:43.133
right after "South Park"
on Comedy Central.

